# Design docs

`design/` holds product law and historical handovers. Prefer code + tests as truth when a doc status line disagrees.

## Living invariants (enforce in code)

From billboard / live notes / ledger docs:

1. Daemon decides interruption; extension only compares billboard id.
2. Not every open shows landing — priority, freshness, ack.
3. Silent hours do not suppress user-initiated landing.
4. Latest is one message, not a notification centre.
5. Cold / warm / hot open tiers; never block first paint; warm ≤4s.
6. Templates first; LLM upgrade only; every model call logged; no secrets in logs.
7. No invented zeros; storage fail-soft; ledger feeds the engine, not a dashboard UI.

## Editing docs

- When implementing a design marked "nothing implemented", **flip the status** in the same PR.
- Handovers are snapshots: on edit, update version/test counts or mark **Historical** at the top.
- Do not add a third mockup source of truth. Canonical UI: extension CSS + AI Usage DS tokens; `design/screens/` and old concept HTML are references unless a task says otherwise.
- ASCII wireframes may still say "AI usage"; when rewriting, use `tokens-go-brrr` for product chrome.
